activity-date.narrative:
The recruited, training and deployment of pre-election long term observers started with sampling of constituencies in Ghana.
The sampling for the pre-election long-term observation (LTO) work started with the grouping of the 275 constituencies under at least one of the criteria below:
I.	Competitive/swing/two major parties stronghold constituency;
II.	Flash points/hotspots constituency;
III.	Border town constituencies; and
IV.	Constituency with female parliamentary candidate(s).

Next, we purposively decided on a target of 100 constituencies for the pre-election LTO. In selecting these constituencies, we ensured that all four criteria above were represented. The process for the sampling involved the following steps:
1.	Purposively included the only constituency that embodied all the 4 criteria;
2.	Purposively included all the 15 constituencies that have 3 of the 4 criteria;
3.	Purposively selected 4 constituencies in the Ashanti Region with 2 of the 4 criteria that are of critical interest to CODEO; and
4.	Randomly distributed the remaining 80 constituencies that have either 2 or 1 of the criteria across the regions based on their percentage shares in the number of constituencies that remained after we have purposively selected 20 constituencies.
